{#
  name: office-map
  purpose: The offices on a map whose dots are links: an inline SVG drawn in the theme's colours that scales to its column, beside the same links as a list (to-do 7; an image map until 0.17.0, whose fixed-pixel hot spots made narrow columns scroll).
  anatomy: shell(center false) > grid > figure(svg[role=group] > a(hit circle + dot + label) per office) + ul > li > a
  data: s = { title, lede, items: [{ title (city), slug, href, address, geo: { lat, lng } }] } (from "offices")
  a11y: the svg is a labelled group naming the offices; each office link has an accessible name ("Office in Hamburg") and a 22-unit transparent hit circle, and shows its focus on the dot and the label; the list repeats the links as text
  i18n: labels come from the locale's office names; the map itself never mirrors (geography)
#}
{% from "sections/_shell.njk" import shell with context %}
{% macro render(s, ctx) %}
{% call shell("office-map", s, ctx, { center: false }) %}
{%- set names = [] %}{% for o in s.items %}{% set names = (names.push(o.title), names) %}{% endfor -%}
<div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-5 lg:items-center">
<figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line lg:col-span-3">{{ s.items | officeMapInline("ui.officeIn" | t, "ui.officeMapAlt" | t | replace("{list}", names | join("ui.comma" | t))) | safe }}</figure>
<ul class="space-y-4 lg:col-span-2">
{%- for o in s.items %}
<li><a href="{{ o.href }}" class="group block rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface-raised p-4 hover:border-brand-300 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus"><span class="block font-semibold group-hover:underline underline-offset-4">{{ o.title }}</span><span class="mt-1 block text-sm text-ink-muted">{{ o.address }}</span></a></li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endmacro %}
